                                        "entry_id": "d2db4c74-09d0-3066-88ac-0634a6b54ef7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curve or bend in a tubular organ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a470d8bc-4a38-4a6d-88fd-41a1ceeff0cb",
                                                "sense_id": "3810c764-8e98-3d36-b981-b35c7fe663c3",
                                                "text": "The Stomach [of a weasel] about three inches long; proportionably, more than a Dogs. An inch in Diametre at the upper Orifice; and the nether, ¼; having a flexure towards its Conjunction with the Guts: ſhaped like to the body of a pair of Bag-Pipes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71ecc9e8-1932-3d1c-b1a8-c1c32671838c",
                                        "entry_id": "d2db4c74-09d0-3066-88ac-0634a6b54ef7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The last joint, or bend, of the wing of a bird."
